{"authored" [{"question" "q-129662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nRequire $D\\subseteq R$, so the rectangle contains the entire region. Which of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [0,2]$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/review.json" "file_sha256" "6d4404b732d0b5cabb493da81288d3f70e8982fe66a473641844b01b3e4793da" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a2421cd6717dc0f82de7aa6a0a8456b75996c62ef9a82913d4be576802f98a7a" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/verification.json" "basis" 1799 "rationale" "Make the verified containing-region interpretation explicit in the study request. The prompt now requires D subset R and the worked solution checks each rectangle against the actual ellipse or displayed domain. Zero extension on a containing rectangle preserves the integral. Keys and complete answer fields remain unchanged; original source, grades and interpretations remain preserved. Equality for a particular integrand alone is not a general containment criterion, illustrated decisively by q129666 odd-in-x cancellation."} {"question" "q-129662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The ellipse $x^2/9+y^2\\le1$ has horizontal extent $[-3,3]$ and vertical extent $[-1,1]$. Rectangles I and II both contain this entire bounding box and thus all of $D$. Rectangle III excludes $(0,-1)$, so it does not contain all of $D$.\n\nOn either containing rectangle, $f=9-x^2$ on $D$ and zero on $R\\setminus D$. Consequently $\\iint_R f\\,dA=\\iint_D(9-x^2)\\,dA$. The answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/review.json" "file_sha256" "6d4404b732d0b5cabb493da81288d3f70e8982fe66a473641844b01b3e4793da" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a2421cd6717dc0f82de7aa6a0a8456b75996c62ef9a82913d4be576802f98a7a" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/verification.json" "basis" 1799 "rationale" "Make the verified containing-region interpretation explicit in the study request. The prompt now requires D subset R and the worked solution checks each rectangle against the actual ellipse or displayed domain. Zero extension on a containing rectangle preserves the integral. Keys and complete answer fields remain unchanged; original source, grades and interpretations remain preserved. Equality for a particular integrand alone is not a general containment criterion, illustrated decisively by q129666 odd-in-x cancellation."} {"question" "q-129662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/review.json" "file_sha256" "6d4404b732d0b5cabb493da81288d3f70e8982fe66a473641844b01b3e4793da" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a2421cd6717dc0f82de7aa6a0a8456b75996c62ef9a82913d4be576802f98a7a" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-129662/verification.json" "basis" 1799 "rationale" "Make the verified containing-region interpretation explicit in the study request. The prompt now requires D subset R and the worked solution checks each rectangle against the actual ellipse or displayed domain. Zero extension on a containing rectangle preserves the integral. Keys and complete answer fields remain unchanged; original source, grades and interpretations remain preserved. Equality for a particular integrand alone is not a general containment criterion, illustrated decisively by q129666 odd-in-x cancellation."} {"question" "q-129662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-3,3]\\times [0,2]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f63a01971bda887285e96077926af" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/4a8671db243a19fb258f6144d6aba1b193e237ef93d45d877829f80b93bc7d36.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle III does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and II cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f63a01971bda887285e96077926af" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1dd6b5880f7162c5e89d5d9a910fa55ae62fc84f22fc6ebcef9e0368d226dae3" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f63a01971bda887285e96077926af" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f6